secondary-background\">Other Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">1.0<br/><span class=\"implementation-date\">January 07, 1997<br/>Alpha 1.0</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\">See also: Objects<span class=\"explained\">Help</span></nav>\n</aside>\n<div id=\"w-twbox-intro\">\n<div id=\"w-object-profile\">\n<div id=\"w-twbox-image\"><img alt=\"latest?cb=20050502223321&amp;path-prefix=en&amp;format=original\" class=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Bag_f395a0.gif\"/></div>\n<div id=\"w-twbox-look\"><div class=\"item-look tibiatext tibiagreen\">You see a bag <span class=\"p-attributes\">(Vol:8)</span>.<div class=\"p-weight\">It weighs 8.00 oz.</div><br/></div></div>\n<div class=\"\" id=\"w-twbox-sounds\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:left;\"></div>\n<div id=\"w-object-notes\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Notes\">Notes</span></h3>\n<p>Players often threw bags on the ground, so you could easily find them all around <a href=\"#/wiki/Tibia\">Tibia</a>. See Bags for more information about other types and colors of bags. It looks the same as <a href=\"#/wiki/Belongings%20of%20a%20Deceased\">Belongings of a Deceased</a>, <a href=\"#/wiki/Belongings%20of%20a%20Deceased%20%28The%20Ravager%29\">Belongings of a Deceased (The Ravager)</a>, <a href=\"#/wiki/Belongings%20of%20a%20Deceased%20%28Death%20Priest%20Shargon%29\">Belongings of a Deceased (Death Priest Shargon)</a> and a Loot Bag (Item).\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:left;\"></div>\n<div class=\"history-section\" id=\"w-object-history\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-History\">History</span></h3>\n<p>They used to be dropped by almost every kind of <a href=\"#/wiki/Creatures\">creature</a>, but this was changed in the 2010 Summer Update.\n</p>\n</div>\n<